Yes, technically they are different.

Applications Accepted is based on the final application status being accepted/complete in the application data.

Booked Accounts would require us to link the accepted application to the credit card account table and confirm that an account was actually opened.

From our latest discussion with James, for the NCMI requirement, “booked cards” is effectively referring to accepted/completed applications, so we are planning to use Application Accept Count and keep the application-to-account / Booked Accounts logic on hold for now.